  KaggleERN: without true_labels.csv (the Kaggle download has none) the
  test set is 4 of the 16 labelled subjects, not EEGPT's 10 Kaggle test
  subjects -- their row is a reference, not the same test data. The
  split's split.json says which ('test_split').

  Preprocessing: our pretraining pipeline (0.5 Hz high-pass, 50 Hz notch,
  per-window z-score). Rows tagged 'eegptprep' use EEGPT's instead on BCIC
  (0-38 Hz low-pass, Euclidean alignment, common average).

  EEGPT's rows: frozen encoder + linear probe, mean over folds, scored on
  their validation subjects. Ours: one fold, test subjects select nothing.
